# Personal data. Never commit these.
#
# Both patterns are unanchored on purpose: a "profile" or "applications"
# directory is private no matter how deep it sits, because a user may run
# cv-kit from a nested working directory.
profile/
applications/

# The worked example is the one exception. Its profile is fictional and the
# README links to it. Git will not descend into an excluded directory, so the
# directory has to be re-included before its contents can be.
!examples/**/profile/
!examples/**/profile/**

# Generated documents, except the worked example's.
*.pdf
!examples/**/*.pdf

# Local-only instructions
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Throwaway venvs used by the page-count fallback
.venv/
venv/
